---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
// Drafted for the operator to personalize (name, sectors, specific platforms
// used). Remove `noindex={true}` when the bio is final.
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who writes this guide, and how it makes money." noindex={true}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <article class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>About this guide</h1>

      <p>
        I've spent more than ten years in institutional fundraising and grant
        work: writing the proposals, running the research, and using many of the
        tools reviewed here in real fundraising programs. Most of that time has
        been in and around education, where budgets are tight and a software
        decision follows you for years.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site organizes fundraising software by shop size, because that is
        what actually determines what you should run. A $400k shop and a $6M
        shop need different stacks, and a recommendation that ignores your
        budget isn't a recommendation.
      </p>

      <h2>How the guide works</h2>
      <p>
        Every price on this site comes from the vendor's published pricing or,
        where pricing is quoted per organization, from ranges vendors and their
        customers report. Every recommendation names the shop size and situation
        it fits. Free tools are covered alongside paid ones, and the strongest
        advice on most pages is the simplest: shortlist two or three tools, book
        the demos, and test each one against your own data. A good demo will
        show you things no review can.
      </p>

      <h2>How it makes money</h2>
      <p>
        Some outbound links are affiliate links. If you start a paid plan
        through one, this site may earn a commission at no cost to you. Several
        tools recommended here pay nothing at all. Recommendations run on fit;
        the links come after. Read the <a href="/disclosure/">full disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Spotted a stale price or a recommendation that missed the mark? Tell me.
        Reader corrections are what keep a guide like this accurate.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
